# /etc/cap/identities.conf — one CAP identity per SSID ("multi-identity").
#
# Copy this file to /etc/cap/identities.conf and restart capagent
# (`/etc/init.d/capagent restart`).  Without this file capagent runs the
# normal single-identity topology and takes every BSS the manager provisions.
#
# Format, one identity per line (blank lines and # comments are ignored):
#
#   tag   identity        radio-mac[,radio-mac...]
#
# Every identity gets its own certificate (/etc/cap/id-<tag>.pem and .key,
# enrolled on first start), ext-auth directory (/var/run/hostapd<tag>), VAP
# journal (/var/run/caps<tag>.state) and hostapd file suffix
# (CAPAGENT_RUN_TAG=<tag>).
#
# The manager needs one provisioning rule per radio MAC, each with
# action=create-dynamic-enabled, master-configuration=<that SSID> and no
# slave-configurations; see docs/MULTI-IDENTITY.md.
#
# MAC rules
# ---------
# * 2.4 GHz (mt7603e): any unique locally-administered unicast MAC works;
#   sharing the first byte is fine.
# * 5 GHz (mt76x2e): the driver derives the BSS index from the first byte of
#   the address.  Every identity that shares the phy MUST use a different
#   first byte, locally administered and unicast: 02, 06, 0A, 0E, 12, 16,
#   1A, 1E, 22, 26, 2A, 2E, ..., 3A, 3E.  Two identities with the same first
#   byte (02 in an early build) leave the second BSS in EBUSY.
# * An identity that drives the second phy advertises two radios: an unused
#   placeholder (radio 0, no provisioning rule) and the 5 GHz MAC (radio 1).
#   Do not use a MAC that another rule claims as a placeholder.
#
# Proven layout: four 2.4 GHz identities on phy0 and four 5 GHz identities on
# phy1, all as masters of their own fake radio.  Change the SSIDs/security on
# the manager; the tags and MACs here only have to match the rules.

# tag  identity       radio-mac(s)
a      OpenWrt-CAPA   02:D1:27:1B:2D:A0                    # 2.4 GHz
b      OpenWrt-CAPB   02:D1:27:1B:2D:A1                    # 2.4 GHz
c      OpenWrt-CAPC   02:D1:27:1B:2D:A2                    # 2.4 GHz
d      OpenWrt-CAPD   02:D1:27:1B:2D:A3                    # 2.4 GHz
e      OpenWrt-CAPE   02:D1:27:1B:2D:B0,2A:D1:27:1B:2D:90   # 5 GHz
f      OpenWrt-CAPF   02:D1:27:1B:2D:B1,2E:D1:27:1B:2D:90   # 5 GHz
g      OpenWrt-CAPG   02:D1:27:1B:2D:B2,22:D1:27:1B:2D:90   # 5 GHz
h      OpenWrt-CAPH   02:D1:27:1B:2D:B3,26:D1:27:1B:2D:90   # 5 GHz
